README
======

This suite translates each language-independent case in case/ into every host
language with ./trans and compares the emitted source against the checked-in
case/<name>_<lang>.rl for that language. Unlike ragel.d, which runs the
translated program, the comparison here is on the source text itself.

What is under test is colm, not the translator. The twelve trans-*.lm
backends and the local ragel.lm are a frozen copy of the translator, taken in
2019 and deliberately not kept in step with the one ragel.d builds: that copy
uses the grammar in src/ragel and has since gained print_off, NFA support and
a renamed machine-name token. With the cases, the expected output and the
translator all fixed, colm and libcolm are the only things that can vary
between two runs, so a difference in the emitted text is a change in colm.

The frozen program is the fixture. Do not regenerate the expected files
against ragel.d's translator: the two would then move together whenever ragel
work touches the backends, and the suite would stop saying anything about
colm. Update the expected files only when a colm change is meant to alter the
output, and read the diff as the record of what changed.

The cost of the arrangement is that the colm language surface exercised here
is whatever the 2019 program happens to use. Features added since are covered
by colm.d, not by this suite.
